sentences.t:
Atque equidem Teucrum memini Sidona venire
finibus expulsum patriis, nova regna petentem
auxilio Beli;

sentences.l:
And indeed I remember that Teucer came to Sidon,
expelled from his native borders, seeking new kingdoms
with the help of Belus;

sentences.t:
Aeneas (neque enim patrius consistere mentem
passus amor) rapidum ad navis praemittit Achaten,
Ascanio ferat haec, ipsumque ad moenia ducat;

sentences.l:
Aeneas (for his fatherly love did not allow his mind
to settle) sends swift Achates ahead to the ships,
to carry these things to Ascanius, and himself to lead to the walls;
